# ThreadSanitizer suppressions
# Suppresses known data-race false positives in third-party libraries.
# Loaded via: TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=$PWD/suppressions/tsan.supp
#
# Format:
#   race:<pattern>    — suppress data race (matched against func/source/global name)
#   thread:<pattern>  — suppress thread leak
#
# * matches any substring. ^ and $ anchor to start/end.
#
# IMPORTANT: Suppressions mask real bugs. Review with the library maintainer
# before adding. When in doubt, run without suppressions and triage.

# spdlog — uses relaxed atomics for hot-pattern formatters (intentional)
race:spdlog::*

# Asio — reactor pattern with intentional concurrent socket access
race:asio::detail::*

# mimalloc — allocator fast paths using relaxed ordering (intentional)
race:mi_
race:_mi_

# GoogleTest — static test registration globals
race:testing::*

# Google Benchmark — static benchmark registration globals
race:benchmark::*
